    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254-a1">

                <pb facs="0552" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg428"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 31.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of the French Reception Committee of the State of New
                                York</hi>,<lb/>69 <hi rendition="#italic">Bible
                            House</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1881-09-03"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September</hi> 3,
                    1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor herewith to inclose for
                    the delegation of the French Government, the family of Lafayette, and the
                    descendants of the Count de Rochambeau, the Count de Grasse, and of such other
                    general officers of the French army and fleet who served in the Yorktown
                    campaign in 1781, as may visit the United States to attend the centennial
                    celebration, a proffer of the hospitalities and courtesies of the State of New
                    York.</p>
                <p>I request that you will cause this invitation to be forwarded to these gentlemen
                    through the proper channel, and have the honor to be,</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN A. KING,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Chairman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
